# The family look, shared by all four RunPodFarm nodes (Task 17): violet,
# because it is RunPod's own colour and is essentially absent from stock
# Houdini, so a farm node is recognisable at a glance in a TOP network.
#
# Colour has to be set here rather than baked into the definition: an HDA
# definition carries no colour at all (verified in Houdini 22.0.368 -- a
# node coloured before createDigitalAsset comes back grey). The shape is
# also written by CreateScript's own opuserdata line, so it survives even
# when this event script does not run; re-asserting it costs nothing and
# means one mechanism failing is not the whole look failing.
#
# The shape itself is hda/nodeshapes/rpfarm.json, which `rpfarm setup`
# copies into <prefs>/config/NodeShapes/ (rpfarm.houdini_local.
# install_node_shape) and `rpfarm doctor` checks for -- Houdini resolves a
# shape by name off HOUDINI_PATH and cannot read one out of an asset. If it
# is missing the node just draws as a plain rectangle.
node = kwargs["node"]
node.setColor(hou.Color((0.549, 0.361, 0.882)))
node.setUserData("nodeshape", "rpfarm")

# Start the once-per-session sync-pod watch. The check used to live only in
# onSetupCook, so between cooks nothing ever looked again and a pod could sit
# for hours. Safe to call from every node: it is a no-op after the first, and
# a no-op without a UI.
try:
    kwargs["node"].hdaModule().startSyncPodWatch(kwargs)
except Exception:
    pass
